    "evidence": "The headline clearly states the contradiction, and the numbered intent→agent→page→payment sequence makes the example understandable across viewports. However, “release-custodied synthetic signatures,” “results artifact,” and “evaluation scope” require domain knowledge, while “Follow the payment” does not say what the user will see next. The payment is marked verified, but the screen does not explicitly connect the retrieved-page manipulation to the changed merchant/payment outcome.",
